      "id": "10-verify-outbound-mirror",
      "action": "Verify the kafka->redpanda flow: for each catalog.* topic, the Redpanda end offset must equal the pre-2 baseline plus the Kafka end offset. Groups ecommerce-product-query-service and ecommerce-category-query-service must stay Stable on Redpanda with lag 0. Stop and report on mismatch.",
      "topics": ["catalog.product.events", "catalog.category.events", "catalog.attribute.events"],
      "direction": {"source": "kafka", "target": "redpanda"},
      "services": ["ecommerce-product-query-service", "ecommerce-category-query-service"],
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "configuration", "reference": "src/ecommerce-infrastructure/environments/local/values/ecommerce-product-query-service.yaml:27-38"},
        {"kind": "configuration", "reference": "src/ecommerce-infrastructure/environments/local/values/ecommerce-category-query-service.yaml:27-38"},
        {"kind": "broker_tool", "reference": "docker exec redpanda rpk group describe ecommerce-catalog-service ecommerce-image-service ecommerce-category-query-service ecommerce-product-query-service"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "11-functional-test",
      "action": "Write `OPERATOR: please run the functional test` and wait for the result. After a pass, repeat the checks from items 9 and 10. The test should change a product (with image), a category and an attribute, and exercise a tenant event. Do not claim the move is lossless or exactly-once. On failure, stop and report.",
      "services": ["ecommerce-catalog-service", "ecommerce-image-service", "ecommerce-product-query-service", "ecommerce-category-query-service", "ecommerce-tenant-service"],
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "reasoning", "reference": "TASK.md: the functional test is run by the operator on request."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "12-keep-mm2-running",
      "action": "Leave container mm2 running. Both flows are permanent while tenant-service and the query services stay on Redpanda. Record what the plan created: the mm2 container; workspace dir mm2/; Kafka topics catalog.product.events, catalog.category.events, catalog.attribute.events, tenant.tenant.events, tenant.tenant.events.dlq and the MM2 internal topics (mm2-configs/offsets/status.redpanda.internal, mm2-offset-syncs.redpanda.internal, redpanda.checkpoints.internal and any others found by listing); Kafka consumer groups ecommerce-catalog-service and ecommerce-image-service; Redpanda topics mm2-configs/offsets/status.kafka.internal and mm2-offset-syncs.redpanda.internal if present. List each one before any later deletion.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "reasoning", "reference": "TASK.md: remove only what you created; the outbound consumers depend on the kafka->redpanda flow for as long as they stay on Redpanda."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "R-rollback",
      "action": "Use this only on a failed check, with the operator's agreement. Before item 8: scale catalog-service and image-service back to 1 with the unchanged ConfigMaps, then stop and remove only container mm2. After item 8: revert config.kafka.brokers to redpanda:29092 in both values files and ConfigMaps, then restart. image-service will then re-read mirrored ProductUpdated events from its old Redpanda offset (duplicates, not loss). Keep the kafka->redpanda flow running until its lag is 0, then stop mm2.",
      "services": ["ecommerce-catalog-service", "ecommerce-image-service"],
      "files": [
        {"path": "src/ecommerce-infrastructure/environments/local/values/ecommerce-catalog-service.yaml", "keys": ["config.kafka.brokers"]},
        {"path": "src/ecommerce-infrastructure/environments/local/values/ecommerce-image-service.yaml", "keys": ["config.kafka.brokers"]}
      ],
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "reasoning", "reference": "The Redpanda groups of the moved services are left intact by item 6, so a revert resumes from their last Redpanda offsets."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "allow_lists": [
    {
      "flow": "redpanda->kafka",
      "source": "redpanda",
      "target": "kafka",
      "topics": ["tenant.tenant.events"]
    },
    {
      "flow": "kafka->redpanda",
      "source": "kafka",
      "target": "redpanda",
      "topics": ["catalog.product.events", "catalog.category.events", "catalog.attribute.events"]
    }
  ]
}

